   My probe caught them mid-chain (in this snapshot some are at (0,0,12), others at (0,9.35), others at (0,4.9)). At each chain node, all agents in the same phase pile up at the exact same position for one frame. At 600x, 1/60 sec of sim time per frame... but the probe samples once every 2 seconds (120 frames) — to catch a 1-frame overlap every 2 seconds would require probability 1/120 per node... but I caught 10 pairs at 4 different chain nodes in a single snapshot. This is because dozens of agents cross the chain every sim hour, and each one spends about 1 frame at each node position. With 40+ arrivals in the window, the probability of catching ≥1 overlap at each node position is high.

