   The reference implementation has the same problem (agents all share the same entrance node, and at high speed they pile up there). The reference was "known good," so this level of artifact is within tolerance for the checker (runtime_check doesn't measure distances). But the prompt explicitly says "don't bunch at the door... give them a small spawn/loiter area to spread them out." So we should do better: spread out the chain traversal.

